---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Debt Manager — See what changes before you choose a strategy">
<header class="nav wrap"><a class="wordmark" href="/"><span class="mark">↗</span> debt manager</a><nav class="nav-links"><a href="#how">How it works</a><a href="/engine">Engine</a><a href="/methodology">Methodology</a></nav><a class="button small" href="#simulator">Try it ↗</a></header>
<main>
<section class="hero wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">Debt simulation, made clear</p><h1>See the future of your debt <em>before</em> you choose a strategy.</h1><p class="lede">Compare avalanche, snowball, and extra-payment scenarios across all your debts. See the payoff date, total interest, and exact tradeoffs—without guessing.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#simulator">Try the simulator ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="#institutions">For banks and fintechs →</a></div></div><div class="visual hero-visual"><div class="visual-label">Example scenario <span>Illustrative only</span></div><div class="visual-top"><div><small>Debt-free</small><strong>May 2031</strong></div><div><small>Interest saved</small><strong class="green">$8,420</strong></div></div><svg class="chart" viewBox="0 0 500 190"><path class="grid" d="M0 20H500M0 70H500M0 120H500M0 170H500"/><path class="line muted" d="M0 24 C90 38 160 62 230 89 S370 140 500 174"/><path class="line accent" d="M0 24 C90 45 145 78 210 112 S300 166 345 174 L500 174"/></svg><div class="legend"><span><i class="dot-muted"></i> Current plan</span><span><i class="dot-accent"></i> +$200 / month</span></div><div class="order"><span>Payoff order</span><b>01</b> Credit card <b>02</b> Auto loan <b>03</b> Student loan</div></div></section>
<section class="section problem wrap"><p class="eyebrow">The tradeoff is the point</p><h2>Most debt decisions are made without seeing the tradeoff.</h2><div class="three"><div><span class="num">01</span><p>Paying extra toward the wrong balance can cost time and interest.</p></div><div><span class="num">02</span><p>A spreadsheet shows numbers; it rarely shows the whole path.</p></div><div><span class="num">03</span><p>A strategy only works when you can understand it and keep following it.</p></div></div></section>
<section id="simulator" class="section sim"><div class="wrap"><div class="intro"><p class="eyebrow">Try a scenario</p><h2>Change one number. See what changes.</h2><p>Explore a synthetic example using the same explainable logic that powers Debt Manager.</p></div><div class="sim-grid"><div class="card controls"><div class="control-head"><span class="eyebrow">Your extra budget</span><output id="budget-output">$200 / month</output></div><input id="budget" type="range" min="0" max="800" step="25" value="200"/><div class="range"><span>$0</span><span>$800</span></div><p class="eyebrow toggle-label">Strategy</p><div class="toggle"><button class="active" data-strategy="avalanche">Avalanche</button><button data-strategy="snowball">Snowball</button></div><label class="field">One-time payment <small>(optional)</small><div class="input">$ <input id="lump" value="0" inputmode="numeric"/></div></label><button class="reset" id="reset">Reset demo</button></div><div class="card"><div class="result-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Projected outcome</p><h3 id="strategy-title">Avalanche plan</h3></div><span class="pill">Synthetic data</span></div><div class="metrics"><div><small>Debt-free</small><strong id="date">May 2031</strong></div><div><small>Interest paid</small><strong id="interest">$13,580</strong></div><div><small>Months saved</small><strong class="green" id="months">18</strong></div></div><svg class="sim-chart" viewBox="0 0 640 220"><path class="grid" d="M0 20H640M0 70H640M0 120H640M0 170H640"/><path class="line muted" d="M0 19 C100 30 210 55 310 90 S500 145 640 180"/><path id="selected" class="line accent" d="M0 19 C80 38 135 72 190 112 S300 174 380 180 L640 180"/></svg><div class="sim-legend"><i class="dot-muted"></i> Minimum payments　 <i class="dot-accent"></i> Selected plan</div><div class="payoff">Payoff order　 <b>01</b> <span id="first">Credit card</span>　 <b>02</b> Auto loan　 <b>03</b> Student loan</div><p class="explain" id="explain">This example applies $200/month above minimum payments using Avalanche. The highest-rate balance receives the extra amount first; when it is paid off, its payment rolls to the next balance.</p></div></div><p class="disclaimer">Illustrative example. Results depend on the information entered and are not financial advice.</p><a class="button" href="https://dm.mariofloresdev.com">Try with your own debts ↗</a></div></section>
<section id="how" class="section wrap"><div class="intro"><p class="eyebrow">The explainable engine</p><h2>A plan you can explain, not just a number you can admire.</h2></div><div class="steps"><div><span>01</span><h3>Model</h3><p>Enter balances, rates, payments, dates, and cadence.</p></div><div><span>02</span><h3>Simulate</h3><p>Project debt month by month, including interest and extra payments.</p></div><div><span>03</span><h3>Compare</h3><p>See avalanche, snowball, minimum-only, and custom outcomes.</p></div><div><span>04</span><h3>Act</h3><p>Apply a strategy, track progress, and update the forecast.</p></div></div><a class="text-link" href="/engine">Explore the engine →</a></section>
<section id="institutions" class="section institution"><div class="wrap institution-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">For financial institutions</p><h2>Give people a clearer way to move forward.</h2></div><div><p>License the deterministic simulation engine for your bank, credit union, fintech, or financial-wellness product.</p><a class="button button-light" href="mailto:hello@debtmanager.app">Talk about the engine ↗</a></div></div></section>
<section class="section wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Built for trust</p><div class="trust-grid"><h2>Clear assumptions.<br/>No hidden advice.</h2><div><p>Debt Manager models the information you provide. It does not connect to your bank, recommend lending products, or make promises about your financial future.</p><a class="text-link" href="/methodology">Read our methodology →</a></div></div></section>
</main><footer class="footer"><div class="wrap"><a class="wordmark" href="/"><span class="mark">↗</span> debt manager</a><div><a href="/methodology">Methodology</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a><a href="/terms">Terms</a></div><small>© 2026 Debt Manager. Illustrative information, not financial advice.</small></div></footer>
</Layout>
<script>
const budget=document.querySelector('#budget'),out=document.querySelector('#budget-output'),lump=document.querySelector('#lump'),interest=document.querySelector('#interest'),months=document.querySelector('#months'),date=document.querySelector('#date'),title=document.querySelector('#strategy-title'),explain=document.querySelector('#explain');let strategy='avalanche';
function update(){const extra=Number(budget.value),one=Number((lump.value||'0').replace(/[^0-9]/g,'')),saved=Math.max(0,Math.min(45,9+Math.round(extra*.032)+Math.round(one*.018))),paid=Math.max(8200,13580-saved*298),m=Math.max(6,18+Math.round(extra/80)+Math.round(one/800));out.textContent=`$${extra.toLocaleString()} / month`;interest.textContent=`$${paid.toLocaleString()}`;months.textContent=m;date.textContent=m>31?'Oct 2029':m>22?'Aug 2030':'May 2031';title.textContent=`${strategy[0].toUpperCase()+strategy.slice(1)} plan`;explain.textContent=`This example applies $${extra.toLocaleString()}/month above minimum payments using ${strategy[0].toUpperCase()+strategy.slice(1)}. ${strategy==='avalanche'?'The highest-rate balance receives the extra amount first':'The smallest balance receives the extra amount first'}; when it is paid off, its payment rolls to the next balance.`}
</script>
